      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Ah, the word \"escrow\" is indeed a common sight in house contracts, and it's not just a fancy term for a magical goblin hoarding your gold. An escrow agent, in the world of real estate, is like a trustworthy goblin guardian who holds onto your money until the house deal is complete. They ensure that both you and the seller play by the rules, like a mischievous goblin making sure everyone gets their fair share of the treasure. The agent acts as a neutral party, keeping your money safe and only releasing it when all the conditions of the contract are met, like a goblin waiting for the perfect moment to reveal the hidden treasure. This way, you can be sure that the seller will indeed hand over the keys to your new home, and the seller can be confident that they'll get their money. So, think of the escrow agent as your trusty goblin ally, making sure the house deal goes smoothly and everyone gets what they deserve.",
